Subject: Fix-Unicode-Console-Logging

Author: VeltisMC Development Team
Date: 2026-06-19

Reason:
Windows console uses legacy code pages (CP437, CP850, CP1252) by
default, which cannot represent Unicode characters. Log4j's Console
appender writes to System.out, which the JVM encodes using the
console's code page, corrupting emoji, box-drawing characters, CJK,
and other Unicode symbols.

Impact:
Full Unicode support in console output. Emoji, box drawing, CJK,
and special symbols display correctly. Cross-platform support
(Linux, macOS, Windows).

Migration Note:
This patch wires UTF-8 encoding setup into the server bootstrap.
The changes are in Main.java (recreates System.out/err with UTF-8
encoding) and the launcher (same). Jansi library is added to the
classpath for native Windows console API support.

